5T16:43:49.660Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-07-30T15:13:26.943Z\"},\"componentType\":\"author\",\"name\":\"Jordan Smith\",\"slug\":\"jordan-smith\",\"url\":\"/authors/jordan-smith\",\"description\":\"[Jordan Smith](https://jordansmith.ink/) is a freelance writer, editor, and author with 10 years of experience reporting on health, wellness and news infused with pop culture trends. She’s interested in how history shapes today’s trends, which she explored in a book she authored for students on the origins, and deception, of reality TV. Her work has also appeared in *Biography*, *Self*, *Peloton*, and *Runner’s World*, among others.\",\"image\":{\"componentType\":\"cloudinary image\",\"sys\":{\"id\":\"39HgdmNp9mPHIemKZ9sZ7W\"},\"slug\":\"jordansmithqoxmhw\",\"altText\":\"A woman with large sunglasses smiles while standing outside in front of orange and yellow leaf trees. She carries a small smiling dog in a backpack.\",\"title\":\"Jordan Smith author photo\",\"credit\":\"Courtesy Jordan Smith\",\"caption\":\"$undefined\",\"orientation\":\"portrait\",\"width\":597,\"height\":892,\"publicId\":\"Jordan_Smith_qoxmhw\",\"url\":\"http://res.cloudinary.com/aenetworks/image/upload/v1765816922/Jordan_Smith_qoxmhw.jpg\"}}],\"readingTimeInSeconds\":\"$undefined\",\"adKey\":\"apluse.hist.topics/worldwarii\"}],\"quotes\":[],\"adKey\":\"apluse.hist.topics\",\"adCategories\":\"$94:props:children:0:props:adCategories\",\"articleName\":\"world-war-ii-end-events\",\"quickFacts\":\"$undefined\",\"quickFactsLogo\":\"$9c:0:props:children:1:1:props:children:1:props:quickFactsLogo\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"RightRail\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"rich-text-section.tsx\"}]]}]]]}]\na9:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"full-bleed-3\",{\"children\":[\"$@c1\"]}]\naa:[\"$\",\"div\",\"main-content-4\",{\"className\":\"i94vss1 i94vss4 g1fwxfnf g1fwxflx g1fwxfzr g1fwxfii\",\"data-name\":\"section\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"g1fwxf4 g1fwxf7 g1fwxfy g1fwxfy8 g1fwxflu g1fwxfm9 g1fwxfn0\",\"data-contentful-field-id\":\"content\",\"data-contentful-entry-id\":\"1Sc3XU8SjCzZZG8wGqfcvQ\",\"id\":\"main-content-4\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"_15il2ffd _15il2ffa a0xfey1 g1fwxfbr g1fwxfc1 _15il2ffl g1fwxfvr _15il2ffj\",\"id\":\"The-Battle-of-Stalingrad-and-Allied-Invasions-Shaped-the-End-of-WWII\",\"children\":[\"The Battle of Stalingrad and Allied Invasions Shaped the End of WWII\"],\"data-sentry-element\":\"H\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"H2\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"heading.tsx\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"_42elsx1 a0xfey3 g1fwxfzv g1fwxfzz\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"After storming across Europe in the first three years of the war, overextended Axis forces were put on the defensive after the Soviet Red Army rebuffed them in the brutal \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/battle-of-stalingrad\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Battle of Stalingrad\"]}],\", which lasted from August 1942 to February 1943. The fierce battle for the city named after Soviet dictator \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"https://www.history.com/topics/russia/joseph-stalin\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Joseph Stalin\"]}],\" resulted in nearly two million casualties, including the deaths of tens of thousands of Stalingrad residents.\"]}],\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"_42elsx1 a0xfey3 g1fwxfzv g1fwxfzz\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"As Soviet troops began to advance on the \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/articles/8-things-you-should-know-about-wwiis-eastern-front\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Eastern Front\"]}],\", the Western Allies \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/invasion-of-sicily\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"invaded Sicily\"]}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/italian-campaign\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"southern Italy\"]}],\", causing the fall of Italian dictator \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/benito-mussolini\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Benito Mussolini’s\"]}],\" government in July 1943. The Allies then opened a Western Front with the amphibious \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"9\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/d-day\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"D-Day invasion of Normandy\"]}],\" on June 6, 1944. After gaining a foothold in northern France, Allied troops \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"11\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/liberation-of-paris-video\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"liberated Paris\"]}],\" on August 25 followed by Brussels less than two weeks later.\"]}],\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"_15il2ffd _15il2ffa a0xfey1 g1fwxfbr g1fwxfc1 _15il2ffl g1fwxfvr _15il2ffj\",\"id\":\"The-Battle-of-the-Bulge-Marks-Germany's-Last-Stand\",\"children\":[\"The Battle of the Bulge Marks Germany's Last Stand\"],\"data-sentry-element\":\"H\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"H2\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"heading.tsx\"}]]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"x4or4w5 x4or4w6 g1fwxfk g1fwxfs\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",\"$Lc2\"]}]]]}]\nab:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"full-bleed-5\",{\"children\":[\"$@c3\"]}]\nac:[\"$\",\"div\",\"main-content-6\",{\"className\":\"i94vss1 i94vss4 g1fwxfnf g1fwxflx g1fwxfzr g1fwxfii\",\"data-name\":\"section\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"g1fwxf4 g1fwxf7 g1fwxfy g1fwxfy8 g1fwxflu g1fwxfm9 g1fwxfn0\",\"data-contentful-field-id\":\"content\",\"data-contentful-entry-id\":\"1Sc3XU8SjCzZZG8wGqfcvQ\",\"id\":\"main-content-6\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"_42elsx1 a0xfey3 g1fwxfzv g1fwxfzz\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Germany found itself squeezed on both sides as Soviet troops advanced into Poland, Czechoslovakia, Hungary and Romania while the Western Allies continued to push eastward. Forced to fight a two-front war with dwindling resources, an increasingly desperate Hitler authorized a last-ditch offensive on the Western Front in hopes of splitting the Allied lines. The \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/articles/battle-bulge-american-defeat-hitler\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Nazis launched a surprise attack\"]}],\" along an 80-mile, densely wooded stretch of the Ardennes Forest in Belgium and Luxembourg on December 16, 1944.\"]}],\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"_42elsx1 a0xfey3 g1fwxfzv g1fwxfzz\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"The German onslaught caused the Allied line to bulge, but it would not break during six weeks of fighting in subzero conditions that left soldiers suffering from hypothermia, frostbite and trench foot. American forces withstood the full might of what was left of Germany’s power but lost approximately 20,000 men in what was their deadliest single battle in World War II. What became known as the \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/battle-of-the-bulge\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Battle of the Bulge\"]}],\" would turn out to be Germany’s last gasp as the Soviet Red Army launched a winter offensive on the Eastern Front that would have them at the Oder River, less than 50 miles from the German capital of Berlin, by the spring.\"]}],\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\"}]]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"x4or4w5 x4or4w6 g1fwxfk g1fwxfs\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"$La6\",null,{\"mainContainerId\":\"main-content-6\",\"relatedArticles\":[{\"sys\":{\"id\":\"5iHVHYkvJgbyv8syper1tl\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-01T22:18:39.034Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-13T20:40:20.007Z\"},\"componentType\":\"article\",\"subComponentType\":\"regular\",\"title\":\"How the WWII Burma Campaign Helped Turn the Tide Against Japan\",\"subHeading\":\"The grueling 1944–45 Allied offensive reopened the crucial overland supply route to China and dealt the Japanese army one of its worst defeats of the war.\",\"homepageHeadline\":\"$undefined\",\"url\":\"/articles/burma-campaign-wwii-road-china\",\"slug\":\"burma-campaign-wwii-road-china\",\"heroImage\":{\"componentType\":\"cloudinary image\",\"sys\":{\"id\":\"6XjUce5zeoJqbW23v9E0HD\"},\"slug\":\"burmacampaign\",\"altText\":\"Men of the British Army's 36th Infantry Division advance through a banana grove, November 6, 1944.\",\"title\":\"The British Army In Burma 1944\",\"credit\":\"Sgt. A Stubbs/ Imperial War Museums via Getty Images)\",\"caption\":\"Men of the British Army's 36th Infantry Division advance through a banana grove, November 6, 1944.\",\"orientation\":\"landscape\",\"width\":5199,\"height\":2924,\"publicId\":\"burma_campaign\",\"url\":\"http://res.cloudinary.com/aenetworks/image/upload/v1782934846/burma_campaign.jpg\"},\"meta\":{\"sys\":{\"id\":\"2jvImfONYXxr1ramn1UYdL\"},\"componentType\":\"meta\",\"title\":\"How the WWII Burma Campaign Turned the Tide Against Japan | HISTORY\",\"description\":\"$undefined\",\"openGraphDescription\":\"The grueling 1944–45 Allied offensive reopened the crucial overland supply route to China and dealt the Japanese army one of its worst defeats of the war.\",\"legacyPublishedDate\":\"$undefined\",\"legacyModifiedDate\":\"$undefined\",\"thumbnailImage\":\"$undefined\",\"adCategories\":[\"Military\"],\"noindex\":false},\"topic\":{\"sys\":{\"id\":\"4bhWOA6U2NK4LN6KKuyZbL\"},\"componentType\":\"link\",\"url\":\"/topics/world-war-ii\",\"text\":\"World War II\",\"slug\":\"world-war-ii\"},\"subtopics\":[],\"collections\":[],\"sponsor\":\"$undefined\",\"authors\":[{\"sys\":{\"id\":\"5JNWDsPEwwsNOz1ysCVWHY\",\"createdAt\":\"2025-06-06T15:13:02.307Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-07-29T10:12:08.941Z\"},\"componentType\":\"author\",\"name\":\"Mark Piesing\",\"slug\":\"mark-piesing\",\"url\":\"/authors/mark-piesing\",\"description\":\"Mark Piesing, a freelance journalist based in Oxford, UK, was a finalist for Media Aviation Awards in both 2024 and 2025. He is author of *N-4 Down: The Hunt for the Arctic Airship Italia*. Learn more at markpiesing.com or follow him @MarkPiesing.\\n\",\"image\":{\"componentType\":\"cloudinary image\",\"sys\":{\"id\":\"4UyjE7OpnEUnxp0Q8aM6VU\"},\"slug\":\"mark-piesing-headshot\",\"altText\":\"The image shows a middle-aged man with gray hair holding up a book titled \\\"N-4 Down\\\" against a dark background.\",