\"Box\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"$La6\",null,{\"mainContainerId\":\"main-content-8\",\"relatedArticles\":[],\"quotes\":[],\"adKey\":\"apluse.hist.topics\",\"adCategories\":\"$94:props:children:0:props:adCategories\",\"articleName\":\"world-war-ii-end-events\",\"quickFacts\":\"$undefined\",\"quickFactsLogo\":\"$9c:0:props:children:1:1:props:children:1:props:quickFactsLogo\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"RightRail\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"rich-text-section.tsx\"}]]}]]]}]\naf:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"full-bleed-9\",{\"children\":[\"$@c5\"]}]\nb0:[\"$\",\"div\",\"main-content-10\",{\"className\":\"i94vss1 i94vss4 g1fwxfnf g1fwxflx g1fwxfzr g1fwxfii\",\"data-name\":\"section\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"g1fwxf4 g1fwxf7 g1fwxfy g1fwxfy8 g1fwxflu g1fwxfm9 g1fwxfn0\",\"data-contentful-field-id\":\"content\",\"data-contentful-entry-id\":\"1Sc3XU8SjCzZZG8wGqfcvQ\",\"id\":\"main-content-10\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"_42elsx1 a0xfey3 g1fwxfzv g1fwxfzz\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"After the \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/battle-of-dresden\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"firebombing of Dresden\"]}],\" and other German cities that killed tens of thousands of civilians, the Western Allies crossed the Rhine River and \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/articles/the-final-push-to-berlin-the-history-behind-fury\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"moved eastward toward Berlin\"]}],\". As they closed in on the capital, Allied troops discovered the horror of the Holocaust as they liberated concentration camps such as Bergen-Belsen and \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"https://www.history.com/topics/world-war-ii/dachau\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Dachau\"]}],\". With both fronts collapsing and defeat inevitable, \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/this-day-in-history/adolf-hitler-commits-suicide\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Hitler committed suicide\"]}],\" in his bunker deep below the Reich Chancellery on April 30, 1945.\"]}],\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"_42elsx1 a0xfey3 g1fwxfzv g1fwxfzz\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Hitler’s successor, Grand Admiral Karl Dönitz, started peace negotiations and on May 7 authorized General Alfred Jodl to \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/this-day-in-history/germany-surrenders-unconditionally-to-the-allies-at-reims\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"sign an unconditional surrender\"]}],\" of all German forces to take effect the following day. Stalin, however, refused to accept the surrender agreement inked at the headquarters of U.S. General \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/topics/us-presidents/dwight-d-eisenhower\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Dwight D. Eisenhower\"]}],\" in Reims, France, and forced the Germans to sign another one the following day in Soviet-occupied Berlin.\"]}],\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"_15il2ffd _15il2ffa a0xfey1 g1fwxfbr g1fwxfc1 _15il2ffl g1fwxfvr _15il2ffj\",\"id\":\"Atomic-Bombing-of-Hiroshima-and-Nagasaki\",\"children\":[\"Atomic Bombing of Hiroshima and Nagasaki\"],\"data-sentry-element\":\"H\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"H2\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"heading.tsx\"}]]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"x4or4w5 x4or4w6 g1fwxfk g1fwxfs\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"$La6\",null,{\"mainContainerId\":\"main-content-10\",\"relatedArticles\":[],\"quotes\":[],\"adKey\":\"apluse.hist.topics\",\"adCategories\":\"$94:props:children:0:props:adCategories\",\"articleName\":\"world-war-ii-end-events\",\"quickFacts\":\"$undefined\",\"quickFactsLogo\":\"$9c:0:props:children:1:1:props:children:1:props:quickFactsLogo\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"RightRail\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"rich-text-section.tsx\"}]]}]]]}]\nb1:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"full-bleed-11\",{\"children\":[\"$@c6\"]}]\nb2:[\"$\",\"div\",\"main-content-12\",{\"className\":\"i94vss1 i94vss4 g1fwxfnf g1fwxflx g1fwxfzr g1fwxfii\",\"data-name\":\"section\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"g1fwxf4 g1fwxf7 g1fwxfy g1fwxfy8 g1fwxflu g1fwxfm9 g1fwxfn0\",\"data-contentful-field-id\":\"content\",\"data-contentful-entry-id\":\"1Sc3XU8SjCzZZG8wGqfcvQ\",\"id\":\"main-content-12\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"_42elsx1 a0xfey3 g1fwxfzv g1fwxfzz\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Even after the \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/articles/v-e-day-around-the-world\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Allied victory in Europe\"]}],\", World War II continued to rage in the Pacific Theater. American forces had made a slow, but steady push toward Japan after turning the course of the war with victory at the June 1942 \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/battle-of-midway\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Battle of the Midway\"]}],\". The Battles of \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/battle-of-iwo-jima\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Iwo Jima\"]}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"7\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/battle-of-okinawa\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"Okinawa\"]}],\" in the winter and spring of 1945 were among the bloodiest of the war, and the American military projected that as many as 1 million casualties would accompany any invasion of the Japanese mainland.\"]}],\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"_42elsx1 a0xfey3 g1fwxfzv g1fwxfzz\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Weeks after the \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/trinity-test\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"first successful test of the atomic bomb\"]}],\" occurred in Alamogordo, New Mexico, on July 16, 1945, \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/topics/us-presidents/harry-truman\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"President Harry Truman\"]}],\", who had ascended to the presidency less than four months earlier after the death of Franklin D. Roosevelt, authorized \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"/topics/world-war-ii/bombing-of-hiroshima-and-nagasaki\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"its use against Japan\"]}],\" in the hopes of bringing a swift end to the war. On August 6, 1945, the American B-29 bomber \",[\"$\",\"i\",\"7\",{\"children\":\"Enola Gay\"}],\" dropped an atomic bomb on the manufacturing city of Hiroshima, immediately killing an estimated 80,000 people. Tens of thousands later died of radiation exposure. When Japan failed to immediately surrender after the \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"9\",{\"href\":\"this-day-in-history/american-bomber-drops-atomic-bomb-on-hiroshima\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"bombing of Hiroshima\"]}],\", the United States detonated an \",[\"$\",\"$La5\",\"11\",{\"href\":\"/articles/hiroshima-nagasaki-second-atomic-bomb-japan-surrender-wwii\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"g1fwxfm3\",\"children\":[\"even more powerful atomic bomb on Nagasaki\"]}],\" three days later that killed 35,000 instantly and another 50,000 in its aftermath.\"]}],\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"_15il2ffd _15il2ffa a0xfey1 g1fwxfbr g1fwxfc1 _15il2ffl g1fwxfvr _15il2ffj\",\"id\":\"The-End-of-World-War-II:-Soviets-Declare-War-and-Japan-Surrenders\",\"children\":[\"The End of World War II: Soviets Declare War and Japan Surrenders\"],\"data-sentry-element\":\"H\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"H2\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"heading.tsx\"}],\"$Lc7\",\"$Lc8\"]]}],\"$Lc9\"]]}]\nb3:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"full-bleed-13\",{\"children\":[\"$@ca\"]}]\nb4:[\"$\",\"div\",\"main-content-14\",{\"className\":\"i94vss1 i94vss4 g1fwxfnf g1fwxflx g1fwxfzr g1fwxfii\",\"data-name\":\"section\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\",\"data-sentry-component\":\"Box\",\"data-sentry-source-file\":\"box.tsx\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"g1fwxf4 g1fwxf7 g1fwxfy g1fwxfy8 g1fwxflu g1fwxfm9 g1fwxfn0\",\"data-contentful-field-id\":\"content\",\"data-contentful-entry-id\":\"1Sc3XU8SjCzZZG8wGqfcvQ\",\"id\":\"main-content-14\",\"data-sentry-element\":\"Component\